{
  "version": 2,
  "name": "CodeTerminal",
  "description": "The source image is drawn with terminal glyphs. Source colour and brightness are sampled once per character cell, keeping whole glyphs at image contours. Brightness controls character illumination and stroke weight; gaps and spaces never fill. Amount brings the terminal in over the image: characters glow on top of the picture first, then the picture under each character fades to black, with cells flickering at the arrival edge and rows tearing sideways while the reveal is in motion. At full Amount the image is entirely terminal. Fresh Text keeps retyping groups of lines with new shell, code, log and memory passages; at zero, still content settles. Source changes trigger local typing and data-character edits. Layout selects Single or tmux-style panes; Activity zero holds the characters.",
